WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:01.660
JEN PERSON: This
week, we're talking

00:00:01.660 --> 00:00:04.180
about Persistent
Disk, BigQuery and SAP

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.100
apps, and AutoML Translation.

00:00:06.100 --> 00:00:08.770
I'm Jen, and welcome
to This Week in Cloud,

00:00:08.770 --> 00:00:12.010
where we serve you the
lowest latency news.

00:00:12.010 --> 00:00:14.110
When it comes to managing
block storage data

00:00:14.110 --> 00:00:16.630
protection in the cloud,
everyone makes trade-offs

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:18.400
based on their situation.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:21.130
To make sure you're ready with
the backup and recovery plan

00:00:21.130 --> 00:00:23.710
that your situation
needs, we've got a variety

00:00:23.710 --> 00:00:26.230
of features in Persistent Disk.

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:29.440
Features like snapshot
locality, scheduled snapshots,

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:31.450
and automatic
replication between zones

00:00:31.450 --> 00:00:34.210
for regional persistent disk.

00:00:34.210 --> 00:00:36.730
BigQuery is a dream come
true for massive data

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.660
sets in machine learning models.

00:00:38.660 --> 00:00:40.900
And now, we're
making complex tasks

00:00:40.900 --> 00:00:43.420
like data quality
checking part of BigQuery

00:00:43.420 --> 00:00:45.490
with the beta launch
of scripting and stored

00:00:45.490 --> 00:00:46.720
procedures.

00:00:46.720 --> 00:00:49.240
Before, steps had
to be run manually.

00:00:49.240 --> 00:00:51.700
But now you can script
directly in BigQuery.

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:53.380
Hello, local variables!

00:00:53.380 --> 00:00:56.590
And even save your script as a
stored procedure, which you can

00:00:56.590 --> 00:00:59.370
share and run again next month.

00:00:59.370 --> 00:01:01.860
Building great cloud
solutions is more than

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.739
building your perfect
enterprise data warehouse.

00:01:04.739 --> 00:01:07.170
Companies rely on
internal data systems

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:10.440
to operate systems
like SAP apps.

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.410
And often, those systems need to
work with your cloud solutions

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.340
to discover new insights.

00:01:15.340 --> 00:01:17.078
So we've got an
integration guide

00:01:17.078 --> 00:01:18.870
that will walk you
through data replication

00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:24.210
from SAP applications to Google
BigQuery with existing tooling.

00:01:24.210 --> 00:01:27.450
Our Translation API got a
series of updates this week.

00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:31.360
Most notably, AutoML Translation
is now generally available.

00:01:31.360 --> 00:01:33.870
So anyone can build
domain-specific translation

00:01:33.870 --> 00:01:35.370
into their workflows.

00:01:35.370 --> 00:01:37.320
Translate your corporate
lingo with the use

00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:40.260
of a glossary or three,
which you can apply

00:01:40.260 --> 00:01:42.030
manually or automatically.

00:01:42.030 --> 00:01:44.147
Talk about synergy.

00:01:44.147 --> 00:01:46.230
If you want to read more
about these announcements

00:01:46.230 --> 00:01:48.480
or see a full list,
check out the link.

00:01:48.480 --> 00:01:50.110
Have any thoughts or ideas?

00:01:50.110 --> 00:01:51.670
Leave us a comment or tweet us.

00:01:51.670 --> 00:01:54.650
We'll see you in the cloud.

